course: dictionary
lesson: 12128
title: Remembering with words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about looking back. When people commemorate something, they remember it and show that it matters, often with a ceremony or a special object. «The town held a parade to commemorate the soldiers who died in the war.» The parade is how the town remembers them.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «A plaque was put on the wall to commemorate the scientist who once lived here.» A plaque is a flat sign, so it is something made to help people remember. The clues point to the meaning, so you do not need to guess.
explain: Commemorate is a verb, so it changes: commemorates, commemorated, commemorating. Try the swap check. «Every November we commemorate Remembrance Day.» Swap in «remember and honour» and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Commemorate means to remember and honour a person or event, often with a ceremony.
fact: «Commemorate» is a verb: commemorate, commemorates, commemorated, commemorating.
fact: A statue, plaque or stamp that commemorates something is made to help people remember it.
fact: «A coin commemorating a famous event» is a coin that helps people remember that event.
fact: Churches commemorate saints on their feast days.
exercise: «The town held a parade to commemorate the soldiers who died.» What does commemorate mean? | To build a new road | To argue about the rules | To forget quickly | *To remember and honour
exercise: «A plaque was put on the wall to commemorate the scientist.» What is a plaque like this made to do? | Keep the rain out | *Help people remember the scientist | Carry water to the garden | Hold up the roof
exercise: Mia says commemorate means forget. Is she right? | Yes, it means to forget something quickly | No, it means to buy something new | Yes, it means to break something | *No, it means to remember and honour something
test: «The stamp commemorates the 100th birthday of the poet.» What is the stamp for? | *To help people remember the poet's birthday | To post letters only | To show that the poet is sad | To hide the poet's name
test: «Last year the school ___ the 50th anniversary of its opening.» Which word fits the gap? | *commemorated | commemorate | commemorating | commemorates
exam: Which word means to remember and honour with a ceremony? | Forget | Demolish | Whisper | *Commemorate
